// The program mega_bare carries in ROM.
//
// Named pins.csp because that is the name Makefile.board looks for -- PROG
// defaults to the board directory's pins.csp -- but it is a whole program, not
// just a pin map: on a board that exists to prove the port runs, a pin map that
// declares two pins and does nothing would prove exactly as much as an empty
// image.
//
// It matches boards/mega_bare/diagram.json: an LED with a 220R resistor on pin
// 13, and a button to ground on pin 2.
//
//   make -f Makefile.board BOARD=mega_bare
//   then F1 -> "Wokwi: Start Simulator"

#digital Led out 13
#digital Btn in pullup 2

// Half a second on, half a second off.
//
// `= 1` starts it at program start. A timer does NOT restart itself -- it fires
// once and stops -- so the rule below arms it again on its own timeout. Leaving
// that out gives one blink and then a board that looks dead.
#timer Blink 500 = 1
Blink = 1 ? timeout(Blink)

// TOGGLE, unless the button is down. The pin has its pullup on, so an open
// button reads 1 and a pressed one reads 0: holding it freezes the LED at
// whatever it was, which is a visible answer to "is the input being read"
// that does not need a second LED to show it.
Led = !Led ? timeout(Blink) && Btn
